         [weight] FLOAT
     )
 
+SQLite 3.37 and higher supports `STRICT tables <https://www.sqlite.org/stricttables.html>`__,
+which reject values that cannot be converted to the declared column type. Pass
+``strict=True`` when creating a table to enable this feature::
+
+    db["measurements"].insert(
+        {"id": 1, "value": 1.5},
+        pk="id",
+        strict=True,
+    )
+
+This option is also accepted by ``.create()``, ``.insert_all()``, ``.upsert()``,
+``.upsert_all()`` and ``.lookup()``. Python ``float`` columns use SQLite's
+``REAL`` type in strict tables. The ``table.strict`` property reports whether
+an existing table is strict.
+
